Nothing amazing about this except that it was my second ascension.
Took me over two years for my first; between my first and second,
three months. May the times continue to diminish. Conduct-wise, it was
polyselfless (I really hate polymorphing myself) and wishing-for-
artifact-less (I didn't need to).

Goodbye Sarah the Demigoddess...

You went to your reward with 3604342 points,
Magicbane (worth 3500 zorkmids and 8750 points)
The Eye of the Aethiopica (worth 4000 zorkmids and 10000 points)
       1 worthless piece of colored glass, (don't ask. I didn't know I
had it either.)
       2 amulets of life saving (worth 300 zorkmids),
and 0 pieces of gold, after 64611 moves.
You were level 18 with a maximum of 129 hit points when you ascended.

High points:

- Started with magic missile, which was lucky already, but then found
a wand of wishing at DL7. It makes the start game a lot easier when
you have lots of nice stuff. (SDSM, speed boots, amulet of life
saving, helm of brilliance, and 2 blessed scrolls of genocide.)

- I manage to make it to Medusa, at level 13, with no Ft. Ludios, no
methods of gaining a level, and no source of levitation. Thus starts a
massive, dungeon-wide ring polypiling effort. Near the end (when
everything is getting system shocked left and right), I finally get
the ring of levitation AND the ring of conflict at once.

- Conflict makes everything easy. The Castle, Gehennom, and Moloch's
Sanctum are no problem. I pay off Asmodeus and Baalzebub. Juiblex
decides not to engulf me (this has never happened before...why now?)
and dies easily. I kill Orcus with a well-timed cockatrice egg. The
Sanctum, too, is perfect. I didn't even get Yeenoghu summoned (which
seems to happen to me a lot.)

- I die once on the Plane of Air to air elementals. The Amulet of
Yendor makes magic missile very difficult to cast. This is also where
I use up my last potion of full healing.

- At the Astral Plane, I forget to take off my ring of conflict. Thus
begins hell. I trudge to the left altar - Ptah. I decide to go to the
right, and it's Anhur. I'm leaving out mass amounts of conflict-
induced carnage and near death experiences.

Dumb moments:

- At the bottom of the mines, a nymph decides to be invisible. I hate
it when this happens. Fortunately, I have two blessed scrolls of
genocide! Unfortunately, I can't remember which letter is nymph and
which is naga, and am nevertheless confident enough not to look it up.
Goodbye, scrolls of genocide I was going to use on liches and deadly
water creatures.

- When selling random crap from the Mines at Minetown, I sell
Magicbane instead. The shopkeeper didn't know what hit him.

- I forget to eat and become fainting on at least four occasions. I'm
lucky I didn't get killed.

- It's time to find the vibrating square. I look all over. No dice. I
look again. Nothing. I dig up the entire middle of the level with a
pick axe. Still nothing. Then, I notice the down stairs.

- I get onto the correct floor and find the square, burn Elbereth with
a wand of fire, drop the bell, drop the candelabrum, and prepare to
apply the candles which I just now realize I forgot.

Miscellaneous notes:

- I hate quest peacefuls, especially when they block corridors I need
to get through.

- I also really hate the Plane of Fire. Not because it's hard, but
because of the fact that you get SO MANY MESSAGES.

- I never found a magic lamp until Orcus Town.

- There was a considerable lack of shops. Not counting Minetown, I
only saw two, and they were small.

- Levitating does not get you out of lava. I learned this the hard
way.

Spells that came in handy:

Force Bolt - I don't like Force Bolt and hate using it, ever since the
time a wand of wishing was glass, and shattered. Nevertheless, it's
how I broke statues and boulders.
Magic Missile - This I like. I didn't really use it as much as I could
have, however. I actually played the wizard more like a fighter,
unless something like a lot of soldier ants or just a lot of enemies
were approaching.
Identify - I actually didn't find this until after the Quest, but it
came in handy then.
Magic Mapping - Gehennom becomes much less tedious.
Dig - For the Plane of Earth, even if the Amulet kept sapping my
energy.
Finger of Death - I didn't get to use this when I needed it (i.e. the
Wizard's reappearing spree) since I had forgotten it by the time I
killed him for the first time, and it was all the way back at my
stash.
Cure Sickness - Pestilence.
Extra Healing - The only reason why I didn't die more than once. I had
a set routine on the Astral Plane. Heal, bash/cast, move, repeat.

